{"type":"message","id":"7ce42d63","parentId":"95f87fc9","timestamp":"2026-04-09T02:36:19.289Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The script runs fine and completes quickly (well under 20 seconds). So the issue isn't with the script itself.\n\nThe timeout must be happening in the cron job execution environment. This could be related to:\n1. The isolated session taking time to start up\n2. Some overhead in the cron job runner\n3. The 30 second timeout being too aggressive for the overhead + script execution\n\nLet me try to update the cron job timeout. Since the openclaw CLI commands seem to be hanging, let me try using the sessions_send to delegate this task, or I could try to edit the config directly.Actually, let me check if there's a way to update the cron via the config file directly. Or I could try spawning a subagent to do this.\n\nActually wait - looking at the earlier output, the commands were running but just taking a long time. Maybe the openclaw CLI is slow to start up. Let me try again with a simple cron command.","thinkingSignature":"ec0d21119ed4d40c664ebe320df18d9efb45a5b2bfc919fb156a65a257910338"},{"type":"text","text":"脚本执行正常，2秒就完成了。问题可能是 **cron job 的 30 秒 timeout 太短**，加上 cron runner 启动 isolated session 的开销。\n\n让我再试一下修改 cron 超时：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_v0xbosxcdk3w_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron edit 2af4bbbc-7d03-40b5-87a3-03e3be36acb7 --timeout-seconds 60 2>&1 &\nsleep 8 && kill %1 2>/dev/null; wait","pty":false,"timeout":12}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":26239,"output":336,"cacheRead":12524,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":39099,"cost":{"input":0.007871699999999999,"output":0.0004032,"cacheRead":0.0007514399999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.009026339999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775702167138,"responseId":"062643970f0152ea2de3e08280d6bf50"}}
